  "norad": 67291,
  "name": "QMR-KWT 2",
  "callsign": "RS95S",
  "modulation": "GFSK9k6",
  "ax25_pid": "0xF0",
  "reference": "https://gitlab.com/librespacefoundation/satnogs/satnogs-decoders/-/blob/master/ksy/sputnixusp.ksy",
  "document": "SatNOGS decoders \"sputnixusp.ksy\" (Kaitai Struct), Sputnix Unified Protocol (same family as UmKA-1, 57172). Record types 0x4246 (UHF beacon) and 0xED21 (5-channel power system) are verified on 3 real frames of the 2026-11-20 IQ recording (UHF time matches the burst time within 1 s, uptime advances 30 s per frame, bit rate field 9600, battery voltage matches the UHF voltage). 0xDE21, 0xDF25 and 0x4216 follow the ksy but no such frame has been received. Units come from the ksy comments; the battery/board temperatures are raw/100 degC by inference (raw -518 would be impossible as degC; UmKA-1 shows +5.7 degC next to a 5 degC amplifier; QMR-KWT 2 shows -5.2 degC next to -2 degC). uhf_rss_rx is 255 (probably 'no signal') in all frames. The PS clock reads 2018-03-02, i.e. it is not set to UTC.",
